# Whitespace grouping

Use blank lines to separate logical groups. Do not pack unrelated steps into one dense block.

Group by meaning, for example:

- setup vs assertions
- success case vs failure case
- early-return checks vs the happy path
- distinct scenarios inside one test

```ts
// ❌ BAD — mixed steps with no breathing room
const result = sure(() => {
	throw "raw";
})();
expect(result.isErr()).toBe(true);
if (result.isErr()) {
	expect(result.error.message).toBe("raw");
}

// ✅ GOOD — construct, then assert
const result = sure(() => {
	throw "raw";
})();

expect(result.isErr()).toBe(true);
if (result.isErr()) {
	expect(result.error.message).toBe("raw");
}
```

Keep tightly related lines together (e.g. two expects about the same value). Prefer one blank line between groups; avoid double blanks.
